    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0112" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Halifax</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President’s Special
                        Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret and personal</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-14">April 14, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Harry</hi>: Anthony has asked me to give you
                    the following message from him:— <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Have you any news for me about very secret matter we discussed?<anchor
                                n="1" xml:id="d8-f1"/> You will realize we have various decisions to
                            take if there has to be separate development.<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d8-f2"/>
                        </p>
                        <p>Kindest regards.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I was proposing to <hi rendition="#italic">write</hi> him a secret word about the
                    larger issues we raised together last night,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d8-f3"/> so
                    that nobody but he would see it, and explain why for that reason you had nothing
                    to say at the present moment. But you may like to send some message of your own
                    in reply to this.</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="1" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>In his account of his visit to Washington in March 1943, Eden, p. 440, mentions
                    that he had some discussions, principally with Hopkins, about the atomic bomb
                    project. There is no mention of these discussions in the American records of the
                    Eden visit.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d8-f2" n="2" xml:id="d8-f2-content">
                <p>The message quoted here is dated April 13, 1943, in Eden, p. 657.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d8-f3" n="3" xml:id="d8-f3-content">
                <p>Hopkins’ conversation with Halifax on the evening of April 13, 1943, is described
                    in Eden, p. 657.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
